  "note": "Annual election of one third, held in May from 1936; there was no Lurgan election in January 1935 (no nominations were reported), and the third elected in January 1932 sat until May 1936. Four of the five retiring members were declared re-elected and the fifth seat was filled by Robert Liggett, a new member. \"All five are Unionists.\" Polling day, had there been a contest, was 15 May 1936."
